  <prompt>Make H13 trap T7 prove that both BFF slots carry ExternalAccess__CustomerBusinessUnitId equal to H10's customer business unit.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer (L2 H13).</role>

  <goal>
    The BFF's external registration (`POST /api/v1/external/registration`) answers 500 `registration_owner_unconfigured`
    without `ExternalAccess:CustomerBusinessUnitId`, and R3 (#1673) makes first-sign-in contact creates depend on it. H4b already
    writes it to both slots from H10's `InterStepState.CustomerBusinessUnitId` (commit `faf36207d`), but nothing reads it back.
    After this task T7 fails a stamp whose slots lack it or carry a different unit.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Source: GitHub #2265 (uac-r2), R3 ISS-005 #1673. Write path: `PerEnvSourceCatalog.cs` source
      `from-h10-output:customer_business_unit_id`, manifest entry (required), DAG H4b ← H10. The Secure Record BU is refused
      structurally at H10 (`CustomerBusinessUnitIntake` refuses its name; the customer unit is a direct child of the root and a
      sibling of the Secure Record unit), so T7 does not look the unit up in Dataverse.
      The T7 probe already reads both slots' app settings (task 238, 255) and, since task 264, the BFF app registration.
      `TrapVerificationRequest` does not carry the customer BU today: add it (H13 builds the request from the run;
      `InterStepState.CustomerBusinessUnitId` is H10's output — declare the read in `HandlerRunInputs` if H13's reads are declared
      there, and keep `RunContextContractTests` green; H13 is a DAG descendant of H10).
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/CustomerIdentityT7Probe.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/IE2ETrapVerifier.cs (TrapVerificationRequest)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/E2EAcceptance/H13E2EAcceptanceGateHandler.cs (request construction)</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Reconciler/HandlerRunInputs.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/Handlers/CustomerIdentityT7ProbeTests.cs</file>
      <file>docs/guides/SPAARKE-CUSTOMER-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md (§9 T7 row, §12.3 check)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/provisioning.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="§11">Extend T7 and TrapVerificationRequest; no new probe, gate, interface or DI registration.</constraint>
    <constraint source="run-context contract">Any new InterStepState read is declared in HandlerRunInputs; RunContextContractTests stay green; never a Gap to pass.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner">No live change. App-setting VALUES are never logged beyond the public GUIDs T7 already reports.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Add `CustomerBusinessUnitId` to TrapVerificationRequest (optional, default ""), set it in H13 from the run's InterStepState, declare the read.</step>
    <step order="2">T7 clause: both slots' `ExternalAccess__CustomerBusinessUnitId` parse as a GUID equal to the run's (case-insensitive GUID compare; `:` and `__` key forms as the existing clauses treat them); Failed when missing / blank / unparseable / different, or when the run has no H10 value. Header OUTCOMES updated.</step>
    <step order="3">Tests (pure Evaluate path + ProbeAsync with the existing fakes); guide rows; dotnet test the control-plane tests.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">T7 Passes only when both slots carry the run's customer BU (and every existing clause passes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: T7 returns Failed for a slot missing the setting, a blank or non-GUID value, a different GUID, and a run with no InterStepState.CustomerBusinessUnitId.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RunContextContractTests and all Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane tests pass.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    <note date="2026-10-22">Created from #2265. The write already exists (H4b, faf36207d); this is the read-back only.</note>
    <note date="2026-10-22">Done (code + tests + guide; no live change). TrapVerificationRequest.CustomerBusinessUnitId, set
      by H13 from InterStepState (HandlerRunInputs: H13 Output, required:false — T7 owns the verdict); T7 fourth clause
      CheckCustomerBusinessUnit on both slots (FindSetting rules: case-insensitive name, GUID compare, ambiguous case-variants
      fail); a run without H10's unit (blank / unparseable / all-zero) fails. The clause is in Evaluate, so a Graph read
      failure (T264 SettingsVerdictOrDeferral) cannot hide it. Remediation: start a new run (a resume does not re-run a
      completed H4b) or the one-line `az webapp config appsettings set`, then H13. Guide §9 T7 row, §12.3 checks, H4b note.
      ControlPlane.Tests 3176 passed, 0 failed, 1 skipped (pre-existing); fail-before proof: 18 of 65 T7 tests fail with the
      check stubbed. Review: one adversarial pass — nothing F-class (BFF binding checked on master: Guid? via BindConfiguration,
      Linux App Service `__` form, no false pass); K3 remediation wording and K4 changelog order fixed. Second full pass not
      run: no F-class finding, fixes are message text + doc order (re-verified by tests). Known limits: K1 T7 does not repeat
      the BFF's Secure Record / default-owner-team checks (H10 structure; header says so); K2 a KV-reference or case-variant
      duplicate value fails T7 although the BFF binds it (manual edits only); K3 the setting name is a literal here and in
      manifest.yaml (a rename fails closed). ACME: its next run's H4b writes the setting before H13 (per-run idempotency), so
      T7 does not fail there for this clause.
      rework: fix-round-1 task 265</note>
  </notes>
